# ⏱️ Quartz

A **Pomodoro-style focus timer** for the Windows terminal, built with .NET 10 and [Spectre.Console](https://spectreconsole.net/).

Quartz helps you stay productive by alternating between configurable focus and break intervals — with progress bars, Windows notifications, and a session history right in your console.

---

## ✨ Features

- **Configurable Focus & Break Times** — set your own durations in minutes
- **Cycle Support** — define a fixed number of focus/break cycles or run in unlimited mode
- **Live Progress Bar** — visual countdown powered by Spectre.Console
- **Pause & Resume** — press `Space` to pause/resume the current timer
- **Quit Session** — press `Escape` to end a session early (with confirmation prompt)
- **Windows Notifications** — balloon-tip notifications at the end of each phase with fun break messages
- **Session Persistence** — every session is saved as JSON to `%AppData%/Quartz/timeline.json`
- **Timeline Stats** — view your session history grouped by month in a styled tree/table view

---

## 📸 How It Works

1. **Start** — enter your focus time, break time, and number of cycles
2. A progress bar counts down each phase (focus → break → focus → …)
3. Windows notifications pop up when phases switch
4. When done (or quit early), the session is saved automatically
5. **Stats** — browse your past sessions in a timeline view, grouped by month

